From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0009] Recover DSML tool calls when the start wrapper token
 is missing (port of vllm-project/vllm#49117, adapted to the c3046d1 base)

WHAT THIS FIXES. At long context, DeepSeek V4 and V3.2 sometimes omit the
opening <｜DSML｜tool_calls> / <｜DSML｜function_calls> wrapper while still
writing a well-formed <｜DSML｜invoke ...> block. The parser only entered
tool mode on the wrapper terminal, so the whole invoke block leaked to the
user as raw DSML text and no tool call was produced -- in both streaming
and non-streaming paths. Upstream tracks this as vllm-project/vllm#48931.

THE FIX (six upstream commits, squashed into one patch here):

1. A new (CONTENT, INVOKE_PREFIX) transition lets a bare, well-formed
   invoke block start a tool call directly from CONTENT. Purely additive
   -- the wrapped path is untouched.
2. A new FOREIGN_BLOCK state: the V4 parser passes a V3.2-style
   `function_calls` wrapper through as plain content and vice versa, so
   neither dialect misparses the other's block. A real tool call that
   starts inside an unclosed foreign wrapper still parses -- the native
   wrapper always wins.
3. False-match guard: the invoke marker has no dedicated special token,
   so prose that merely quotes it (`<｜DSML｜invoke name="...">`) could be
   misparsed as a call. A recovered call now holds its events until the
   name completes, then commits only if the request declared that exact
   tool name; otherwise the held text is released unchanged as content.
4. The hold gives up the moment the buffered text can no longer grow into
   a declared name, so quoted prose streams out promptly instead of
   stalling until the response ends, and a genuine wrapped call that
   follows quoted prose still parses.
5. Recovery is skipped when the request declares no tools, or when
   `tool_choice` is "none". The declared-name set refreshes every
   request, so nothing carries over on a reused engine instance.
6. Text after a recovered call, previously discarded, is now returned as
   content -- padding immediately after the call is held back first so
   inter-call spacing still matches the normal wrapped path.

WHY THIS BASE-SPECIFIC PORT. PR #49117 (vllm-project/vllm, open at port
time) targets vanilla upstream `main`; this repo's parser/tool-call files
(`vllm/parser/*`, `vllm/parser/engine/*`, `vllm/tool_parsers/utils.py`)
come from the `haosdent/vllm@dsv4-flash-a100` lineage this patch series is
pinned to (c3046d1). Every touched region was diffed line-by-line against
a pristine c3046d1 checkout and found byte-identical to the PR's context
under the surrounding code -- only line offsets differ, from unrelated
commits on either side. This patch carries the PR's unmodified logic
renumbered for c3046d1; production code only (test files are upstream's
own suite and don't apply to this tree's test layout).

